{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.Sl2ProlongationRecurrence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.Sl2ProlongationRecurrence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.End"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.sl2_prolongation_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.sl2_prolongation_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/sl2-prolongation-recurrence.lean#L27-L35","doc":"**Symplectic ⇒ one-parameter recurrence.** If the 2×2 prolongation\noperator `B` satisfies the `SL₂` Cayley–Hamilton relation `B² = τ • B − 1`\n(`det B = 1`, `τ = tr B`), then its powers — and hence the prolonged\nperiods `a n = φ(Bⁿ v₀)` — obey `a_{n+2} = τ · a_{n+1} − a_n`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:sl2-prolongation-recurrence","label":"prop:sl2-prolongation-recurrence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/sl2-prolongation-recurrence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}